1
00:01:39,759 --> 00:01:41,600
Pumpkin, corn, and cod pasta.

2
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,720
Cod is rich in protein

3
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:48,080
and amino acids needed for a baby's growth and development.

4
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,440
Pasta as a staple food

5
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,170
can help babies exercise their chewing ability.

6
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,600
It's sweet and delicious.

7
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:56,729
It tastes great too.

8
00:01:56,759 --> 00:02:00,090
Why did you suddenly think of talking about pregnancy food?

9
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:03,760
I'm pregnant.

10
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,930
That's a good thing.

11
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:20,079
That's great.

12
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,780
You should rest early.

13
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,850
I have to submit my draft tomorrow.

14
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,720
I'll continue working on it.

15
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,920
This is a problem that every man

16
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,890
striving for his career might encounter.

17
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,000
I thought if I held on for a few more months,

18
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,530
I could give her a good life.

19
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:42,240
But reality always turns around suddenly when you hold on to hope,

20
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,280
crushing all your dreams into heartbreaking pieces.

21
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,040
We really time-traveled.

22
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,600
It's not even five o'clock now.

23
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,680
I just got here.

24
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,540
You guys haven't arrived yet.

25
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,520
You must not meet yourself.

26
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,000
Why?

27
00:03:33,079 --> 00:03:34,540
The grandfather paradox.

28
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,560
If two of you meet,

29
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,880
you will fall into the gap of time and space and disappear.

30
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,280
If you want to change all this,

31
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,940
you must bypass the other you.

32
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:43,600
Then,

33
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,440
can't I even give myself a heads-up?

34
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,440
It took me three time travels to realize

35
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,370
that I ignored an important thing.

36
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,640
Without a murder weapon,

37
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,280
there can be no murder.

38
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,600
This note

39
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,610
is what you picked up when you first came here.

40
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,040
Although the copyright doesn't make money this time,

41
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,200
after I help you secure the Xinghe Award,

42
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,160
making money in the future will be a piece of cake.

43
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,920
I've completely fallen into a loop,

44
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:33,080
just like Marat.

45
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,360
Then if we come back,

46
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,880
can we really change what has already happened?

47
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,760
When it grows up,

48
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,440
will it jump up and bite me?

49
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,920
If you dare to bite me...

50
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:43,560
I'll kill you.

51
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:47,240
Mr. Dai.

52
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,040
You're always joking.

53
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:52,800
If this were made into a movie,

54
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,200
it would definitely be a big hit.

55
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:56,080
Give me a role then.

56
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,680
Consider it done.

57
00:04:59,480 --> 00:04:59,960
Mr. Dai.

58
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,640
Who is playing the piano?

59
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,440
An old friend.

60
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,160
Step inside

61
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,200
and look at my collection.

62
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,000
Come, come.

63
00:05:41,159 --> 00:05:42,690
Let me bandage you up first.

64
00:05:46,159 --> 00:05:47,360
Do you still remember

65
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,280
why we broke up?

66
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,360
Going back to your own world

67
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,500
might be the right choice.

68
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:02,120
It seems you've forgotten everything.

69
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,400
Have you also forgotten

70
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,640
that we once had a child?

71
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,480
I haven't forgotten.

72
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,240
I often dream about her.

73
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,060
I dream that she's grown up

74
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,810
and looks a lot like you.

75
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,840
She sleeps in a

76
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,240
tiny coffin,

77
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,760
sleeping so peacefully.

78
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,360
I want to hold her,

79
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,120
but she suddenly wakes up

80
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:41,920
and grabs my hand.

81
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:44,680
She says

82
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,680
she will come back to be our child.

83
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,520
I often wonder,

84
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,480
if I had given birth to her,

85
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,960
what she would look like now.

86
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,840
It's all in the past.

87
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,200
Yeah.

88
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,240
I was the one who gave up on her first.

89
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,040
Xiaofei.

90
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,960
At this point in time,

91
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,290
Xiaofei is still alive.

92
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,680
If Xiaofei's ending can be changed,

93
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,130
does it mean our ending can be changed too?

94
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:38,000
Then let's split up.

95
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,580
I'll take care of Xiaofei.

96
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,360
You deal with the helmet guy.

97
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:45,100
Remember, you must never meet yourself.

98
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,800
This is crazy.

99
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,800
They acted so fast.
